A||N||5||bHooper||Emergency! Emergency! Frozen Caliper on a driver! Need help quick!||||4||
Z||000000||bHooper||05-11-2000||07:07 PM||||My budy jsut got his GT inspected and was comming by my house when he had the right front caliper seize on him.  The rotor will not turn.<P>How do we fix this?  I need to know ASAP. tonight!<P>Thaks,<BR>Hoop||||reg||4
Z||000001||theogre||05-11-2000||07:21 PM||||There is no safe temporary fix. you replace the caliper or rebuild it. <P>If you get really lucky, you can release the thing by pressing the brake pedal as hard posible then whack the caliper. If the jam cause is a rust ball this Might pop it loose. Then you can get the thing off to replace it. Otherwise you'll have to try to press it with a really big C clamp. Don't try to depress it all the way. Just enough to get it off the rotor.<P>Either way you'll need to replace that caliper. When they jam it usually means the pistons are wrecked. maybe the bore too.||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||05-11-2000||07:40 PM||||Slap a rebuilt caliper on, bleed it, you're on your way again. That's the best fix.||||reg||1
Z||000003||bHooper||05-11-2000||09:23 PM||||we freed it with a c clamp and will replace the caliper manyana.<P>needless to say, my buddy was dissapointed because he finally got his car taged and inspected for the first time in a long time.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||05-12-2000||09:31 AM||||GA brakes.||||reg||1
